%SIXMD 1
# @?MKSWAP - PROVISION RESERVED AUXSTORE SWAP SPACE

## DESCRIPTION

MKSWAP IS THE PLANNED NATIVE PROVISIONING COMMAND FOR EXPLICITLY
SELECTED DSK OR DRM AUXSTORE REGIONS.  IT IS NOT YET INSTALLED.
THE CURRENT HOST-SIDE MK AUXSTORE IMAGE UTILITY IS NOT A NATIVE
REPLACEMENT AND DOES NOT OPERATE ON LIVE CONTROLLERS.

THE NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION MUST PROVIDE READ-ONLY INSPECTION AND
DRY-RUN, EXACT CONTROLLER, UNIT AND BLOCK-RANGE SELECTION, AND
EXPLICIT DESTRUCTIVE CONFIRMATION.  IT MUST REFUSE EXISTING FORMATS,
NONEMPTY REGIONS, OVERLAPS AND UNKNOWN OR INVALID DEVICE LAYOUTS.
NO AUTOMATIC FORMATTING MAY OCCUR DURING BOOT.

## @?FILES

### @?AUXST1
ON-MEDIA AUXSTORE VERSION 1 DESCRIPTOR IN PHYSICAL BLOCK ZERO.
THE DESCRIPTOR DEFINES BACKSTORE, LOGSTORE AND CACHESTORE RANGES
AND OPTIONAL CO-RESIDENT D6FS PARTITION METADATA.

